<title>USA: Sony unveils &quot;world's smallest camcorder&quot;.</title>
<headline>Sony unveils &quot;world's smallest camcorder&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PARK RIDGE, N.J. 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Corp's Sony Corp of America said Tuesday it had launched what it described as the smallest digital Handycam camcorder with a screen in the world.</p>
<p>The company said the DCR-PC7 Digital Handycam, brought to the market by Sony Electronics, is as small as a passport.</p>
<p>It said the digital video format camcorder weighs about one pound without the tape or battery and measures 2-1/4-inches wide, 5-1/2 inches high and 4-1/2 inches deep.</p>
<p>The camcorder, which features a color screen and viewfinder, is to become available in November at a suggested list price of $3,199, it added.</p>
